<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wanyan Xiyin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1140</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wanyan Xiyin was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jurchens">Jurchen</a> noble and minister of the Jin dynasty, a kinsman of its founder <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizu-of-jin">Aguda</a>. At Aguda's command he created the Jurchen script in 1119, combining elements of Chinese characters and the Khitan scripts, which was used for government documents and translations of Chinese classics. He also commanded in the wars against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song</a>, and was executed during a court struggle in 1140.</p></div>
